        "anchor": "tools/qwen35_text/main.cc:138",
        "fact": "Recipe::constant freezes only an unfrozen buffer, records kBorrow with original StorageOwner/ReadLease; Recipe::weight deduplicates named weights within the one logical family. Loader-produced weights already have ready leases, so freeze does not allocate another buffer."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "src/graph/executable.cc:1851",
        "fact": "bind_constants stores original tensor views and retains kBorrow owner/lease. needs_canonical_constant only demands a separate canonical owner for an additional physical storage instance or explicit materialize policy."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "src/compute_provider_ggml_cuda/ggml_cuda_provider.cc:732",
        "fact": "Native recipe constants are external roots. Each gets bridge::binding_buffer metadata and binds cuda::detail::const_pointer(original storage); this path does not ggml_backend_tensor_set the raw weight payload."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "src/compute_provider_ggml_cuda/native_bridge_impl.h:331",
        "fact": "binding_buffer sets owns_payload=false and initializes context with nullptr; bind_buffer installs the existing device pointer. Extra ggml handles are not extra full weight allocations."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "src/graph_provider_ggml_cuda/ggml_cuda_region.cc:1225",
        "fact": "Routes3/5 import original BF16/transposed RHS boundaries without packing. Other routes may prepare immutable expressions or pack a qualifying matrix; generic packing is guarded by actual layout, immutable ownership and prepared artifact cache keys."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "src/graph_ggml_shared/constant_packing.h:197",
        "fact": "For MatMul packing, the input must be plain dense and its transpose must not already be dense. Qwen linear explicitly permutes original dense [N,K] to metadata [K,N] RHS, so its usual RHS is already the correct physical orientation and does not create a second dense weight bank."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "src/graph_provider_ggml_cuda/constant_expressions.h:218",
        "fact": "Constant expression payloads allocate only prepared frontier values. Family-local key names original roots, actual View offsets, folded node IDs, descriptors and frontier, preserving dtype/rounding and preventing invalid alias sharing."
      },
      {
        "anchor": "src/graph/executable.cc:10072",
        "fact": "One ConstantArtifactCache packing is used across all finite children. Separate reports/slots can retain the same original raw payload and same proven prepared artifact rather than duplicating ownership capacity."
      }
